## Method law (student-facing)

Five evidence categories (Lesson 1):

| Category | Evidence |
| --- | --- |
| Technical contribution | Drawings, prototypes, experiments |
| Collaborative labor | Lab records, roles, correspondence |
| Legal ownership | Patents, assignments, licenses, courts |
| Financial control | Investment, equity, mergers |
| Public attribution | Ads, biographies, museums |

Three levels (both lessons): **artifact · system · political economy**.

Five Edison case groups (attribution investigations, not “five thefts”):

1. Incandescent lighting (system beyond the bulb).
2. Phonograph (stronger Edison contribution case — do not erase it).
3. Motion pictures (Dickson; Kinetoscope vs projection).
4. Radio (**counterexample** — not an Edison invention claim).
5. Motion Picture Patents Company (market organization / access).

Lesson 2: same questions of Fuller; vocabulary lab (synergy, integrity ≠ tensegrity, ephemeralization, comprehensive design); housing stakeholders; Edison–Fuller matrix; “Dymaxion Without a Genius”; software transfer (specific product + claim).

